def reverse_words(s: str) -> str:
    chars = list(s)
    n = len(chars)
    def rev(i, j):
        while i < j:
            chars[i], chars[j] = chars[j], chars[i]
            i += 1; j -= 1
    rev(0, n - 1)
    i = 0
    while i < n:
        while i < n and chars[i] == ' ':
            i += 1
        j = i
        while j < n and chars[j] != ' ':
            j += 1
        rev(i, j - 1)
        i = j
    return ''.join(chars)
```
The two-pass reverse-then-reverse-words pattern runs in O(n) time and O(n) space for the char list.

